  "id": "COMPOUND:31394 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Azadiradionolide appears to have a shared target of SNU-387, which is a key molecule involved in the biological activity of multiple compounds. SNU-387 is a known target of several compounds, including Bungeiside A and Thelephantin K, all of which have been linked to MOVP-3 as their target. This suggests that Azadiradionolide may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the same downstream pathways or molecular processes that are targeted by Bungeiside A and Thelephantin K. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Azadiradionolide's interaction with SNU-387 is likely to be part of a broader network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of MOVP-3. The consistent targeting of SNU-387 across different compounds supports the idea that Azadiradionolide may exert its effects through a mechanism that is broadly applicable to the class of compounds targeting this molecule.",
